<!--
  A trimmed capture of a real Megaphone-hosted FPL podcast feed, kept because
  two of its properties broke the parser and would break it again silently:

  * pubDate carries "-0000". RFC 5322 says that means UTC with an unknown local
    offset; Python's email parser signals it by returning a NAIVE datetime, and
    the strict "no naive dates" rule then rejected every episode. The feed
    returned 200, parsed cleanly, and yielded zero items.
  * Show notes are a wall of block tags with no sentence punctuation between
    them, so without a block-to-break rule the last word of one bullet fuses
    with the first of the next.

  The fourth item has no pubDate at all and MUST be dropped: a claim with an
  unknown publication instant cannot be tested for admissibility, and an
  untestable claim is indistinguishable from a post-hoc one.
-->
<rss version="2.0" xmlns:itunes="http://www.itunes.com/dtds/podcast-1.0.dtd"
     xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/">
